 certainly done that and I  will say listen you had your your skill  set is vast including braiding your  daughter's hair every time I see that  picture it just makes me smile that's  growth and I and I think whether it's  learning how to braid my daughter's  beautiful hair or whether it is it is  growing to accept my own blind spots  that growth mindset is so important  yesterday  reddit got the message and added tech  CEO Michael Seibel to the board but  couldn't you have if you'd wanted to  just said we're going to add a black  person to the board did you have to step  down I think there is something symbolic  about someone in my position stepping  aside as a way to say we're not just  going to make sure that that you have a  seat at the table I'm gonna give up my  seat so that you can have it I do  believe in in what that represents and I  hope it makes boardrooms all across the  country look around the table and say  who are we serving who is our community  Ohanian says more diversity is in the  best interests of Reddit in the tech  industry more broadly reddit has faced  criticism because hate speech has not  been moderated in the message boards on  the platform but Ohanian venture capital  company initialised has been investing  in new startups that will target hate  online I think if we follow this  drumbeat of support both offline and  online I think we're gonna see more and  more tech businesses in particular  taking more responsibility over not just  the content on their platforms but also  the diversity of their workforces as you  know there are very few black faces in  the boardroom so you thought about that  too and your own experience Alexis in a  boardroom yeah there's this striking  double standard because I have never  walked in a room and not felt a hundred  percent confident be there not felt a  hundred percent welcomed there at times  when I really shouldn't have been  because of my inexperience or because of  my youth or because of my whatever but  that is the privilege that I have locked  my entire life there are things that I  do that my wife checks me on that I'm  doing with the best of intentions but  still require me to feel that pain and  then dig deeper and I'm wondering what  does she helped you see that you didn't  see before there are situations where I  default  fact to be heard because all of my life  when I bring something up I'm generally  in a position where someone is going to  hear me take my side and trust what I  have to say and I take that for granted  and it's not until I am you know talking  to my wife about things that I really  understand that that is not a luxury she  has had do you think that you would have  come away around to this way of thinking  if you had not been with Serena in  particular hmm I would love to say yes  but to see look to have that front-row  seat to her not just her greatness but  everything she has to endure much of it  that never gets reported on that no one  sees right that made the education come  really quickly especially when this is  someone you love but Alexis is you know  nobody likes to be called out people get  very defensive yeah that seems to be  changing but I think it is it is  changing that discomfort that we feel  physically when we push ourselves to go  further is something that we usually  embrace right we know that that's where  growth happens that's where muscles are  tearing just a little bit so they regrow  stronger these conversations are that  same kind of exercise they're that same  kind of discomfort for our brains and  for our souls because at the end of the  day if what we're asking is privileged  white people to be able to feel a little  bit of discomfort to have a hard  conversation that's it's a very  reasonable ask yeah Alexis Ohanian is  saying Lena and white people lead in  enjoyed the discomfort I really  appreciated his candor and he's walking  the walk and talking to talk the first  million in his and his profits in his in  his the first million will go to Colin  Kaepernick's know your rights  so he's pledging his future reddit gains  and the first million because he  believes that Colin Kaepernick is  someone who has transcended his sports  and will show that he's on the right  side of history  so Tony I really enjoyed talking to him  I really appreciated the candor that he  said that he had if you notice on the  wall in the room  did the interview it said pain is gross  pain is girls he believes that I did  notice that I did notice that he's  really comfortable with being  uncomfortable and wants others to be as  well the symbolism is so big right now  it is not going to be enough to have the  best of intentions it's not going to be  enough to follow the golden rule and  treat everyone the same if we are going  to fix the problem of inequality it's  gonna have to take intention and action  Anthony and I think Alexis is really  putting it on the line for the rest of  us to say look it's gonna be sacrifices  well yeah I mean I think his point about  stepping down as a way of showing we're  not just willing to give a seat on the  board to a black person we're willing to  give up our seat to allow a black person  in very symbolic it doesn't sound like a  big difference but it's actually a huge  difference I think Gail oh you're so  right Anthony it's huge and the reaction  from the tech world in the business  community says has been very positive  he's gotten a lot of calls from people  saying how did you do what to do that  they want to engage so I think it's very  important he's sending quite a strong  message thank you very much Alexis  Ohanian

